    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI get the following popup whenever I type something semantic with [glsl-analyzer](https://github.com/nolanderc/glsl_analyzer).\nMini is the latest on main and glsl-analyzer is v1.7.1.\n```lua\nE5108: Lua: ...vim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1261: attempt to index local 'details' (a userdata value)\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                             \n        ...vim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1261: in function 'lsp_completion_response_items_to_complete_items'                                      \n        ...vim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:476: in function <...vim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:426>                   \n```",
